  {
   "post_type": "answer",
   "post_id": 34847499,
   "parent_id": 34847051,
   "author_user_id": 3555525,
   "author_display_name": "Rishikesh Raje",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": false,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/34847499",
   "score": 0,
   "created_utc": "2016-01-18T04:50:01Z",
   "last_edit_utc": "2016-01-19T05:31:04Z",
   "last_activity_utc": "2016-01-19T05:31:04Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "<p>When you say <code>stack = new_Stack(5);</code> you are calling malloc once. and storing the result in <code>stack</code>.</p>\n\n<p>When you call <code>delete_Stack(&amp;stack);</code> you are calling free 5 times on <code>stack[i]</code> and then another free on <code>stack</code>.</p>\n\n<p>This is not required. For this <code>new_stack</code> you just need to call free once. This function will work properly with the given <code>new_stack</code></p>\n\n<pre><code>void delete_Stack (long ** spp) {\n  free((*spp)-STACK_NUM);\n  *spp = NULL;\n}\n</code></pre>\n"
  },
  {
   "post_type": "comment",
   "post_id": 57435238,
   "parent_id": 34847051,
